fication\n\n* For every \\(n\\ge3\\) the values \\(k=0\\) and \\(k=1\\) are realizable (Section 1).  \n* For \\(n\\ge4\\) the value \\(k=3\\) is realizable (Section 1).  \n* No even \\(k\\) can occur (Section 2).  \n* The case \\(k=2\\) is a special even case, hence impossible.  \n* For odd \\(k\\ge5\\) a covering would require a covering of \\(T_k\\) by \\(k\\) sunny lines, which is impossible by Section 3.\n\nConsequently\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{\n\\begin{aligned}\n&\\text{if }n=3:\\qquad k\\in\\{0,1\\},\\\\\n&\\text{if }n\\ge4:\\qquad k\\in\\{0,1,3\\}.\n\\end{aligned}}\n\\]\n\nThese are exactly the non‑negative integers \\(k\\) for which there exist \\(n\\) distinct lines satisfying the two conditions of the problem. ∎"
